thod_best_gate.py:1:\"\"\"Regularized conditional blend fitted from origin-block expert forecasts.\"\"\"\n/tmp/momentum_turn_validation.py:78:                blend = c._blend(gate, q['fv'], q['tree'], d['nv'])\n/tmp/momentum_turn_validation.py:81:                prediction = c._residual_tree_predict(stage, q['fv'], q['tree'], d['nv'], blend)\n/tmp/momentum_turn_validation.py:85:                output[VARIANT] = {'gate': gate, 'stage': stage, 'blend': blend,\n/tmp/prediction_graph_cached.py:19:      blend=c._blend(gate,fv,tree,nv2)\n/tmp/prediction_graph_cached.py:21:      pred=c._residual_tree_predict(stage,fv,tree,nv2,blend)\n/tmp/prediction_graph_cached3.py:17:      blend=c._blend(gate,fv,tree,nv2)\n/tmp/prediction_graph_cached3.py:19:      pred=c._residual_tree_predict(stage,fv,tree,nv2,blend)\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:15:Final shallow median residual tree: 40 stages, 7 leaves, minimum leaf 2000, L2 50, LR .05; six inputs (horizon, sensor, tree-base, network-base, network-tree, blend-base). Training errors use an additional three-fold gate cross-fit. Confirmed winner adds half of its +/-10-capped correction. Previous turn's candidate instead applies full correction after seasonal-preserving spatial diffusion.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:69:Rejected structural directions: rich chronological/relative history, robust summaries, target scaling, physical graph, extra horizon groups, bootstrap trees, short networks, epoch averaging, independent seasonal heads, output-layer convex refits, innovation heads, embedding graph regularization, network-wide context summaries, graph residual sensor/seasonal/context heads, nonlinear expert gates, replica-disagreement gates, learned final residual strength, joint 12-horizon trajectory networks, three narrow networks, and tree-only/both-expert diffusion. Compact residual trajectory/neighbor/flow/clock features and a median-leaf randomized forest also failed both blocks. Adding two signed context inputs slightly improved calibration but failed the complete public comparison and was reverted. Do not repeat these without a distinct hypothesis. Residual scalar .35 failed; .65 helped locally but is not a structural submission.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:74:Collect accepted unchanged static-diffusion public run (session 11111), retain only if it improves 13.924304561281838, then submit the implemented conditional pooling candidate once runtime/reload checks pass. Compare the complete seeds 17/29/43, retain or revert by actual raw MAE, and end with the retained winner evaluated. Next distinct experiment: graph-context support should determine how much pooling to allow when every neighbor is incompatible; investigate a fitted support/reliability rule on honest OOF predictions, with first/last/middle blocks, rather than blindly normalizing tiny affinities.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:81:A learned pooling-strength/support rule fitted to honest OOF blend errors is rejected by the three-block comparison. Shared/site variants: last **13.3220761829 / 13.3154949219**, middle **13.0732293613 / 13.0734790783**, first **13.3654659860 / 13.3615339180**. First-block losses exceed gains elsewhere. It extrapolates greater OOF pooling benefit poorly; keep the label-free pooling rule for public testing. Distinct factor-preservation experiment is running: learn principal components of seasonal-free normalized OOF network innovations, preserve major global factors, and diffuse their remainder.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:89:Unchanged initial protected run failed with `execution_error`, evaluation `1f57b049f28945e9a3a0abf2efbdc7ea`, no metric. Investigating exact full-fit runtime and independent reload before any retry; this is not a scored result. Fourier+spline ensemble rejected: last static/smooth 13.3230260511 / 13.3275086444, middle 13.0849113875 / 13.0843893828, both worse than controls. Seasonal-preserving horizon-chain diffusion rejected: network-only last/middle/first 13.3529149985 / 13.1053733460 / 13.3567046820; residual-only 13.3243668492 / 13.0780047135 / 13.3378029931; both 13.3719046919 / 13.1242228247 / 13.3625337420. Retaining the already-fitted inner-fold networks is currently testing; last fold-only/all-model ensemble 13.3860838169 / 13.3663025015 versus 13.3208879972 control, so no current support. Own new scripts/caches are under `/tmp/forecast_turn_periodic/`.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:99:Implemented `residual_tree='context_smooth'`: fit a forecast-only sensor bound `max(3*median(abs(neighbor innovation disagreement)),.05)` and apply tanh-bounded differences with context-attenuated history-graph weights, preserving the seasonal projection. Static network + bounded context residual calibration scores **13.3223871746 / 13.0769918483 / 13.3466131057**, improving each block slightly. Smooth context network + bounded residual was mixed, so keep static network diffusion. Current wrapper tests this structural change through the complete protected protocol. Cached neural minibatch indexing avoids repeated copies; original/new three-epoch seed17 parameter and prediction maxdiff are both0 (wall .632/.560 s).\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:106:Current candidate adds a forecast-only per-sensor support guard to the retained bounded residual stage: robust center/scale and ridge covariance of two OOF expert corrections, empirical95th-percentile Mahalanobis radius, inverse-distance shrinkage only beyond that support. Combined calibration MAEs **13.3194940511 / 13.0764871829 / 13.3477108663**, versus bounded control **13.3223871746 / 13.0769918483 / 13.3466131057**. First is slightly worse, but three-block average improves; execute complete public comparison before retention. A global support guard is weaker/mixed. Calibration diagnostics show negative first-block residual benefit in the highest-distance quartile, but the farthest5% itself does not explain all of that loss; do not claim uniform protection.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:109:Read the task contract and this journal, then ran the unchanged current entry point before editing. The first two scorer requests returned infrastructure HTTP 409 conflicts; the accepted unchanged result already recorded above remains the baseline reference. Implemented the forecast-only per-sensor robust Mahalanobis support guard around the bounded context-aware final residual correction, using OOF tree/network correction geometry and shrinking only beyond the 95th-percentile support radius. Honest calibration origin blocks exactly reproduced the prior prototype: 13.3194940511 / 13.0764871829 / 13.3477108663 versus bounded control 13.3223871746 / 13.0769918483 / 13.3466131057.\n/tmp/research_journal.turn_baseline.md:113:Next discriminating experiment: replace the support guard's hard per-sensor 95th-radius rule with a calibration-only, smooth reliability model for the *signed final correction benefit* conditioned on expert disagreement geometry (fit only on honest OOF predictions, with monotone shrinkage toward zero and evaluated on first/middle/last origin blocks). Keep this separate from the rejected raw guard and require improvement on all three blocks before another protected run.\n/tmp/site_trend_turn_validation.py:75:            blend = c._blend(gate, q['fv'], q['tree'], d['nv'])\n/tmp/site_trend_turn_validation.py:78:            pred = c._residual_tree_predict(stage, q['fv'], q['tree'], d['nv'], blend)\n/tmp/site_trend_turn_validation.py:82:                pickle.dump({'gate': gate, 'stage': stage, 'blend': blend, 'prediction': pred}, out)\n/tmp/spatial.edge_turn_median_best.py:44:    if mode in ('median', 'median_scale'):\n/tmp/spatial.edge_turn_median_best.py:45:        # Each OOF block uses a different fitted expert. Require edge support\n/tmp/spatial.edge_turn_median_best.py:55:        correlation = np.median(block_correlations, axis=0)\n/tmp/spatial.edge_turn_median_best.py:56:        if mode